### 4.6 Map Companion Metadata File (`.gunzmeta`)

Every time a resonance map is successfully produced, a full implementation **shall** also write a companion metadata file with the same base name and extension `.gunzmeta`. Minimal‑profile implementations (see §1.2) are exempt from this requirement.

**Purpose** – captures the exact evaluator configuration, scan parameters, environmental context, and AI‑facing feedback signals. Not required for map import; enables reproduction, audit, and autonomous decision‑making.

**Format** – valid UTF‑8 JSON with sorted keys, no trailing commas. The canonical serialisation for cryptographic signatures shall follow **RFC 8785 (JSON Canonicalization Scheme)**. Mandatory keys:

| Key | Type | Description |
|-----|------|-------------|
| `gunz_version` | string | `"3.80.0"` |
| `map_fingerprint` | string | XXH3‑128 fingerprint (32 hex digits, lowercase) |
| `creation_timestamp` | string | ISO 8601 UTC with millisecond precision |
| `session_id` | string or null | A unique identifier for the exploration session. If `callback_sandboxed` is `true` (Full profile), `session_id` **MUST** be a non‑null UUIDv4 string (RFC 4122); otherwise (Minimal profile) it may be `null` or any string. |
| `callback_sandboxed` | boolean | `true` if all `PURE_CALL` callbacks in this scan were executed in a sandboxed environment; `false` otherwise. Only `true` or `false` are permitted; any other value causes the metadata file to be rejected. Canonical maps must have this set to `true`. |
| `sandbox_type` | string | (Required if `callback_sandboxed` is `true`) The sandboxing mechanism used. |
| `attestation_signature` | string | (Required if `callback_sandboxed` is `true` and Full profile) An Ed25519 signature over the canonical JSON of the metadata, **after first setting the `attestation_signature` field to an empty string (`""`) and then canonicalising the resulting object**, base64‑url‑encoded, produced by the runtime's attestation key. See §4.10 for the complete procedure. If `callback_sandboxed` is `true`, this field must be present and contain a valid signature; a missing or malformed signature causes the map to be considered non‑canonical. Minimal‑profile implementations may omit this field entirely. |
| `runtime_id` | string | (Required if `callback_sandboxed` is `true`) A unique identifier for the runtime instance that performed the scan. |
| `tool_version` | string | Runtime identification |
| `plan_parameters` | object | All evaluator and scan parameters used for this map.  See **Plan parameters object** below. |
| `drift_enabled` | boolean | (Optional) `true` if the drift metric was computed for this scan.  Absent or `false` otherwise. |
| `scan_zones` | array | Evaluated and excluded zones.  Each element is an object containing: <br> – `freq_low` (integer) – zone start (10⁻⁵ Hz). <br> – `freq_high` (integer) – zone end. <br> – `excluded` (boolean, optional) – `true` if the zone was excluded by the global iteration pre‑pass; absent or `false` otherwise. <br><br> The following fields **MAY** also be present for fully evaluated zones; they are omitted for excluded zones and are entirely optional: <br> – `min_score` (integer) – minimum saturated score in the zone. <br> – `max_stability_width` (integer) – maximum stability width (0.0001 Hz units). <br> – `max_jitter` (integer) – maximum jitter observed in the zone (base time units), **before saturation** to the `u8` field. <br> – `max_advance_regularity` (integer, optional) – The maximum per‑jitter‑point advance regularity observed across all candidates in the zone, expressed in ticks × 100. The value is taken directly from the raw full‑precision integer computed at each jitter point before any averaging across points and before saturation to 65535. It represents the single most extreme instantaneous advance irregularity encountered anywhere in the zone. <br> – `candidates_avoided` (integer) – number of candidates marked `FLAG_AVOID`. <br> – `candidates_skipped` (integer) – (Optional) number of candidates marked `FLAG_SKIPPED`.  For any evaluated zone this count is always zero. |
| `long_term_scan` | boolean | *(Retained for backward compatibility; must mirror `plan_parameters.long_term_scan`)* |
| `time_unit` | integer | Decimal exponent (same as header) |
| `chain_window_duration` | integer | (Optional) If present, the cumulative measurement window across all scans in the same `session_id` chain, expressed in the same base time units as the map header. |
| `chain_next_fingerprint` | string | (Optional) XXH3‑128 of next map in temporal chain |
| `chain_sequence` | integer | (Optional) 0‑based index in chain |
| `map_entries_after_consolidation` | integer | (Optional) Final number of map entries after run‑length consolidation. |
| `map_size_bytes` | integer | (Optional) Total size of the `.gunzmap` file in bytes (header + entries + optional extension). |
| `stats_fingerprint` | string | (Optional) XXH3‑128 of companion `.gunzstats` or `.gunzstatz` file.  The fingerprint is computed over the complete statistics file, including all fields of the **96‑byte records**, using `XXH3‑128` with seed 0. |
| `scan_cost` | object | (Optional) deterministic record of scan resource usage, containing: <br> – `cpu_time_ms` (integer; non‑negative) <br> – `evaluator_iterations` (integer; non‑negative) <br> – `candidates_evaluated` (integer; non‑negative) <br> – `windows_chained` (integer; non‑negative) <br> – `fuel_consumed` (u64; fuel units, reflecting the actual HALT decrement) <br> – `elapsed_time_ms` (u64, optional) – elapsed real time of the scan from start to finish, as measured by a monotonic system clock.  This value is **not** deterministic; identical scans may produce different measurements. <br> – `memory_high_water_mark_bytes` (u64, optional) – peak arena memory used during the scan. |
| `resonance_quality` | object | (Optional) deterministic summary of scan findings.  The following optional fields **MAY** be present: <br> – `max_per_block_advance_regularity` (integer) – The largest per‑block advance regularity observed across all blocks and candidates in the scan, expressed in ticks × 100.  Computed as described in §3.11.  Zero or absent if not computed.  Without drift, this value equals the per‑jitter‑point pooled advance regularity. |
| `system_info` | object | (Optional) host machine details |

